The Constitution of Zimbabwe comes from Veritas (www.veritaszim.net):

  Veritas, Constitution of Zimbabwe: as enacted (Act 1 of 2013, Word .docx) and consolidated as amended up
  to 30 September 2018, 7 May 2021, 20 June 2023 and 28 July 2026 (Word .doc), https://www.veritaszim.net,
  retrieved 2026-10-28; Act 6 of 2026, SI 117 of 2026 and the titled list of 2023 statutory instruments,
  retrieved 2026-10-29.

Licence, as Veritas states it on every page of its website: "This work is licensed under a Creative Commons
Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International License" (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0).
CC BY-NC-SA 4.0: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/legalcode

Attribution:

  Source: Veritas (www.veritaszim.net), licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike
  4.0 International licence (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0).

Veritas's own disclaimer: "Veritas has made every effort to ensure that this updated Constitution is reliable,
but cannot take legal responsibility for any errors."

The other acts come from ZimLII (Zimbabwe Legal Information Institute, on the Laws.Africa Peachjam platform):

  ZimLII, https://zimlii.org, point-in-time versions of each act, read from archived copies of its pages on the
  Internet Archive (https://web.archive.org), retrieved 2026-10-29.

Licence and terms, as ZimLII states them (terms of use s. 9): CC BY-NC 4.0, crediting ZimLII as the source.
CC BY-NC 4.0: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/legalcode

Attribution:

  Source: ZimLII (https://zimlii.org), licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0
  International licence (CC BY-NC 4.0).

The texts may be used only for non-commercial purposes, and material adapted from Veritas must be shared under
the same licence. This repository is private; whether and how it may be published is the owner's decision under these
terms.

Changes made by Lexifina: each edition was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph per
line; spacing, quotes, dashes and list bullets were normalised; Veritas's amendment notes, footnotes, Chapter
and Part headings were left out; the as-enacted text was laid out in the lines of the later editions; and the
editions were arranged as git commits credited to the laws Veritas names for each change. The wording of the
law was not changed. ZimLII acts were treated the same way, with ZimLII's editorial notes as the credit evidence.
Neither Veritas, ZimLII nor Laws.Africa endorses this repository.

The Constitution's provision files, being adaptations of Veritas's editions, are shared under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0;
the other acts' provision files under CC BY-NC 4.0. Lexifina's own
contributions that are not adaptations of those editions (the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
